BT 1 0 0 1 0 65.5 Tm 15.5 TL /F2 12 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Figure 3. PIP-based power versus empirical FDR under single-coding architectures.) Tj /F3 12 Tf ( Rows show additive-only, dominant-only, and recessive-only effects; columns show PVE. Blue) Tj T* (denotes SuSiE and pink SuSiE-mix. Within each panel, all usable simulations with K=1,...,5 are pooled, giving one curve per method. At each PIP threshold, TP and FP counts are) Tj T* (summed before calculating power as TP divided by all causal SNPs and empirical FDR as FP/\(TP+FP\). Thus empirical FDR is a pooled false discovery proportion, not the mean of) Tj T* (per-dataset FDPs. Curves follow decreasing PIP thresholds, with the no-discovery endpoint set to \(0,0\). The displayed empirical-FDR range is 0-0.25. Codings are combined within) Tj T* (components to obtain one mixed PIP per biological SNP. Each dataset has 500 donors; curves have no uncertainty bands and do not establish formal FDR control.) Tj T* ET
